# Copy to .dev.vars for local development. Wrangler loads it automatically and it is
# gitignored, so the key never reaches the repository.
#
# The ePay partner key. This is the credential that opens /public/api/v1/partner/*,
# and it is a different tier from a merchant API key — a merchant key gets 403 on
# partner routes. ePay provisions it when the partnership is established; there is no
# endpoint to create or rotate one.
#
# One key serves both environments. Which environment a merchant transacts in is
# decided per access token, not per key.
EPAY_PARTNER_KEY="..."

# Where ePay should send webhooks. Must be a domain approved on the merchant's point
# of sale, so for local testing this needs a tunnel rather than localhost.
APP_URL="http://localhost:4321"

# Eyga company API. Production uses the private EYGA_API service binding instead.
# Keep the token in .dev.vars or a Worker secret, never in this file.
# EYGA_API_BASE_URL="https://api.eyga.fo"
# EYGA_API_TOKEN=""

# Transactional bank requests. Verify betal.fo in Resend before using this sender.
# RESEND_API_KEY=""
# RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# RESEND_BASE_URL="https://api.resend.com"
# BANK_EMAIL_FROM="Betal <banki@send.betal.fo>"

# Klintra Skriva. Empty means the Undirskriva step can preview a filled FO PDF
# but will not create a signing request. Do not put a real password here.
# SKRIVA_BASE_URL="https://klintraelectronicsigningapi.azurewebsites.net"
# SKRIVA_EMAIL=""
# SKRIVA_PASSWORD=""
# SKRIVA_TENANT_ID="" # optional when the user belongs to exactly one tenant

# Base64-encoded 32-byte AES key for verified P-tal returned by Samleikin.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# IDENTITY_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""
